    "brief": "FIELD FROM CURVES\r\nA field can be generated in a variety of ways. In this example,\r\nthe distance of a curve from the grid points is used to define\r\na field. This creates a field which places parts following the curve,\r\nand \"thickens\" the aggregation along the curve by increasing\r\nthe number of parts.",
